# Apple design rules (stack-neutral)

Reference: https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/
User's brand and instructions win. If a rule conflicts, follow the user and mention it in one line.
Do not copy Apple trademarks, fonts or icons.

## Principles
Clarity, deference (content is the hero), depth with purpose, clear hierarchy, consistency, accessibility first, user control, instant feedback.

## Layout
- 4px scale: 4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 32, 48, 64.
- Mobile-first, flexible layout (flex/grid/clamp). No break at 320px or 200% text.
- Safe areas: `env(safe-area-inset-*)`. Margins 16px phone, 24px tablet, centered max-width on desktop. Text lines 60-75 chars.
- One primary action per screen.

## Typography
- Stack: `-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "SF Pro Text", Inter, system-ui, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif`.
- Few text styles. Body 16-17px, nothing under 12px. Use rem/em. Hierarchy by size and weight. No thin weight on small text.

## Color
- Semantic tokens only (--bg, --text, --accent, --danger...).
- Contrast 4.5:1 text, 3:1 large text and UI parts. Never color alone.
- Dark mode from the start with `color-scheme: light dark` and its own tokens. Honor `prefers-contrast`.

## Interaction
- Touch target 44px (24px absolute floor), 12px spacing around bordered controls.
- All states: default, hover, focus-visible, pressed, disabled, loading. Visible focus ring.
- Verb labels. Destructive actions need confirm or undo. Gestures always have a visible alternative.
- Full keyboard support. Do not hijack scroll, zoom or back.
- Forms: visible labels, right input types, autocomplete, inline fix-it errors, keep input on error.

## Navigation
- Phone: bottom tab bar (3-5). Desktop: sidebar or top nav. Current location always clear. Modals short, closable, never stacked.

## Liquid Glass / materials
- Only on floating controls and navigation, never the content layer. No glass on glass. Use sparingly.
- Legibility first. Clear glass only over rich media, add about 35% dim if media is bright.
- Fallback for `prefers-reduced-transparency` and no `backdrop-filter`.

## Icons and images
- One icon family and weight. SVG. `alt` for meaningful images, `alt=""` for decorative. Sharp on retina.

## Motion
- 150-300ms, transform/opacity only. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (fade or none). No flashing over 3/sec. Autoplay must be pausable.

## Copy and accessibility
- Short, plain, verb-first. Errors say how to fix. Support localization and RTL (logical CSS).
- Semantic HTML first, ARIA to fill gaps, accessible name on every control, headings in order.
- Do not auto-dismiss UI on timers.

## Before finishing
Hierarchy clear, spacing on scale, no overflow at 320px, contrast OK in light and dark, 44px targets, all states, reduced motion and transparency handled, alt text and labels present.
